    private action Quorum3_0_6
        Subsection("Quorum 3.0 June 30th, 2015")
        Card()
        Paragraph("Quorum 3.0 represents the most significant change to the Quorum programming language since its inception and is a near-complete rewrite. When the Quorum project first began, it was written in Java, was interpreted, and we were really just trying to make programming a little easier. As of 3.0, the project has gone further than we ever imagined: Quorum is now faster, robust, and written in itself. As is a long tradition in programming language design, once a language is sufficiently powerful to write the next version in itself, so-called self-hosting, it is a sign that the language is becoming increasingly mature. On Quorum, we have finally reached this milestone and will now be shifting our attention to improved library and development environment support. Library requests to the team, or contributions, are welcome.")
        Paragraph("We had a number of technical goals in mind for the Quorum 3.0 release. We highlight some of the most significant alterations below:")

        Subsubsection("Standard library changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Game Engine 1.0: Quorum now supports a computer gaming engine (in OpenGL). In the first release we are supporting 2D graphics and basic 3D sound (through OpenAL). The design of the system was inspired in part by the excellent LibGDX project. Some of the major features include:")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("OpenGL 2D graphics. The OpenGL aspect is wrapped using LWJGL for efficiency and is used similarly to other toolkits on the market.")
        ListItem("Event handling (e.g., keyboard, mouse)")
        ListItem("Font rendering through the FreeType font libraries.")
        ListItem("Open AL support for audio. In this first release, we support .ogg and .wav files. This library replaces (and upgrades) the existing sound libraries.")
        ListItem("A game creation architecture. This includes a variety of support classes to try and make it easier to create computer games.")
        ListItem("Automatic collision detection support.")
        ListItem("Basic support for texture atlases (ImageSheet objects in Quorum speak).")
        ListItem("A significant amount of documentation and curricular lessons designed to help people learn how to program games in Quorum. Some of this material will come out on the June 30th release, while more will trickle out over time as we write it.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("Lego NXT robotics toolkits are now supported. Specifically, we now support connecting to lego robot kits, which can be used for a wide variety of purposes. Most major functionality in the lego kits are supported.")
        ListItem("Removed support for Botball robots. We feel as if this library was generally not used much by the community and have decided to cease support. Continuing support for this would have required us to re-tool the system to support the new Botball kits, but we decided to focus time on Lego instead, as these kits are cheaper and more popular.")
        ListItem("Included a wide variety of small changes or improvements to the standard library. Many of these came about due to the bootstrapping process, or teaching Quorum to compile itself.")

        Subsubsection("Integrated Development Support changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Sodbeans has largely been rewritten from scratch. The reason we did this is because we largely had to, given the new compiler.")
        ListItem("The module system used by Quorum has been significantly condensed. This will make the update process easier in the future.")
        ListItem("Accessibility Support is now in its own module. A new Accessibility preferences pane provides a variety of new accessibility options.")
        ListItem("Speech now works in IDE on Mac OS X.10, even for components that do not read properly in JDK8 or NetBeans. This is only true if self-voicing is active.")
        ListItem("Several bug fixes to the Quorum debugger have been implemented compared to the 4.6 release. This includes fixes for efficiency as well as user interface improvements.")
        ListItem("The IDE experience has been significantly improved, with much more responsiveness from Quorum generally.")
        ListItem("Integrated an Image Sheet Generator for the new game engine. This generator allows the user to automatically generate ImageSheets in IDE to simplify the process compared to kits like LibGDX, where the process can be somewhat confusing.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug related to the IDE using too many CPU cycles after a number of runs of Quorum.")
        ListItem("Changed all API calls to use the new Quorum 3 implementation, with relatively little supporting Java code in the IDE. This should make it easier to port Quorum to other IDEs, for those that prefer different systems.")
        ListItem("Improved the project user interface in the properties window of Quorum projects.")
        ListItem("Added support to wrap in custom plugins or jar files into Quorum projects. Users should only do this if they know what they are doing, but this new system provides a much more convenient method for connecting between Java, C/C++, and Quorum, including full access to the JDK, C libraries, etc.")

        Subsubsection("Major language changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Quorum now uses an ANTLR 4 backend. Many compiler phases in the language are now considerably faster, thanks largely to Terence Parr's clever work.")
        ListItem("Quorum's type system has been significantly revised, removing some inconsistencies and significantly simplifying tiling/opcode generation. This approach is also somewhat more efficient than in previous releases and works for any future cross-compiling we have planned (e.g., Quorum to Javascript converters).")
        ListItem("Quorum's exception (called Errors in Quorum) system has been redesigned from the ground up. In the new approach, users will always see Quorum errors, never the Java/other equivalent, providing a unified approach.")
        ListItem("Quorum can now generate Java bytecode directly using the excellent ASM bytecode library. Others can use this library for bytecode generation as well. The entire JDK spec is not supported in our hooks to ASM, as we started with features specific to the Quorum compiler, but quite a bit is supported.")
        ListItem("Quorum's backend now supports a number of potential formats, not just the Java Virtual Machine. In post 3.0, we plan to create a first additional backend with a Quorum to Javascript converter. A prototype using this technology can be found at quorumlanguage.com in our hour of code tutorial. Updates and more libraries will be supported over time.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug in Quorum 2.0 that didn't allow us to support action chaining (e.g., a:b():c()). Code completion is not yet finished for chained values.")
        ListItem("A significant optimization pass has occurred for programs generated in Quorum, making programs have faster execution and bootup times under some circumstances.")
        ListItem("Quorum is now fully written, and compiles in, itself. In other words, Quorum 3.0 was compiled in Quorum 2.2 (and then 3.0). The final version of Quorum 3.0 is compiled in Quorum 3.0.")
        ListItem("Quorum's compiler error messages have been redesigned using evidence gathered by Lee and Ko as a loose guide. More work is needed here, as the language and messages are different than Lee/Ko's, but it's a potential improvement until more or better evidence is found.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug in the way Quorum handles inheritance, which ultimately changes how plugins are written. While users generally do not have to use this system, this causes any hidden variables written by the compiler to have slightly different names (e.g., $Interface to _). Also, because of this change, variables, actions, and classes can no longer have an underscore as its last character.")

        Subsubsection("Type system/variable changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Removed a number of cases where Quorum was being slightly "):DoubleQuote():Text("too flexible"):DoubleQuote():Text(" in its conversions between various types, especially in regard to auto-boxing.")
        ListItem("Fixed several issues where Quorum was making strange decisions in what it was allowing users to do (e.g., action Test returns text would allow return false).")
        ListItem("Fixed issues with not being able to pass undefined values to text fields under some circumstances.")
        ListItem("Fixed a couple bugs with how fields and variables were implemented in bytecode.")
        ListItem("Carefully adjusted the amount of type inference allowed on the inside of actions. The value is somewhat conservative and needs to be evaluated in empirical studies. Currently, we know of no randomized controlled trials on how much inference to allow. Users that do have evidence from randomized controlled trials should get in touch with our team on the mailing list.")
        ListItem("Made auto-boxing as transparent as possible, with the hopes that we can eventually disallow use of capital letter types (e.g., Text vs. text).")
        ListItem("In almost all cases now, actions can be called, and chained, on primitive values without any auto-boxing. In other words, calling actions on primitives is quite efficient in Quorum, as values have low memory footprints, but yet still "):DoubleQuote():Text("look like"):DoubleQuote():Text(" calls to objects in other languages, even though they technically are not. Users should not notice a difference with previous releases, with the exception that chaining is allowed.")
        ListItem("Significantly redesigned the testing for the type system, with future improvements in mind. Especially, we have been designing programs to auto-generate test cases that ensure each part of the type system is properly exercised, where, importantly, we can regenerate the entire suite if a change to the type system is made (hopefully with corresponding evidence).")

        Subsubsection("Exceptions (Error) system changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("This system has been fully redesigned. This is a backend change and does change how user's use errors. It does, however, make the system work considerably better.")
        ListItem("In the new system, Quorum Error classes, must inherit from Error, and only, Error. The reason is due to a quirk in Quorum's inheritance system. This is a potential issue that needs further study, but allows the runtime system to have considerable flexibility in how it handles errors.")
        ListItem("Errors generated by the underlying backend are now caught and automatically converted to Quorum style. This allows us flexibility in the system, so that we can study aspects of it in future empirical studies. Previously, we could not modify these internal aspects, giving us too little wiggle room when designing empirical studies to study this system.")
        ListItem("Detect blocks can still contain multiple types (e.g., detect e is CastError), but the compiler now guarantees these are unique. the Quorum 2.0 branch was intended to work similarly, and was close, but this fixes a few edge cases.")
        ListItem("Detect blocks may now be rewritten to a new location by the bytecode generator. This will not impact the semantics of a program, but we have it in the notes in case it is confusing to someone that looks at the generated bytecode.")
        ListItem("Leaving off a type for a detect block makes it automatically of type Error, which is now a catch-all for all possible kinds of system or Quorum errors. This error is guaranteed to be written last in the bytecode generation. In other words, any block of type Error is written last and catches any and all errors, even if these errors were generated by the underlying virtual machine.")
        ListItem("Users that find a Java/other error that gives an error message that is difficult to understand should email the mailing list. These issues are easily adjusted now without changes to the compiler itself.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug that caused Quorum to run forever and need to be killed if an exception occurred in a generated program.")
        ListItem("Adjusted the API for the Error classes making them more consistent, generally, and also making them conform to more modern naming schemes used in Quorum. For example, previous studies showed the word "):DoubleQuote():Text("output"):DoubleQuote():Text(" was more intuitive than "):DoubleQuote():Text("print,"):DoubleQuote():Text(" so this release changes PrintStackTrace to OutputStackTrace. Obviously, the difference is pretty minor, but increases consistency overall.")
        ListItem("Considerably improved the stack trace information presented from errors.")
        ListItem("Errors do not now have a corresponding interface type generated, unlike all other Quorum classes in bytecode. The reason is because of the way Java handles exceptions in regard to its inheritance hierarchy (e.g., Throwable and below).")

        Subsubsection("Control Structure changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("If statements now properly short circuit. This was a bug in Quorum 2.")
        ListItem("Included a number of optimizations at various points in the control structure pipeline.")
        ListItem("Simplified the bytecode generation for various kinds of expressions.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug in if statements that, under very rare circumstances, caused a bytecode verification error.")

        Subsubsection("Compiler Support")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Added preliminary support for the ASM bytecode library to Quorum. This initial version is somewhat bare bones in this first release, but still is sufficient to implement much of a modern compiler built on JDK 7 or 8. Teams interested in using Quorum to generate bytecode that need additional support are encouraged to get in touch, as generating bytecode in Quorum is relatively easy (so far as bytecode writing goes).")
        ListItem("Added parsing/semantic analysis libraries for Quorum. Others can inherit from these and garner full ANTLR 4 support for reading Quorum source")
        ListItem("All symbol tables, analyzers, and generators are public and easily modified for those wanting to write support for Quorum into IDEs or tools, either online or offline.")
        ListItem("Bytecode generation/semantic analysis is now done in two-passes, which simplifies finding/fixing bugs and the generation process compared to the Quorum 2 branch.")
        ListItem("Added a new test suite architecture for compiling and running a large set of cross-compiled Quorum programs. Currently, the system supports programs converted from Quorum to Java Bytecode and JavaScript.")

        Subsubsection("Other changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Fixed a host of minor bugs throughout the language.")
        ListItem("Considerably improved Quorum's automated test suite generally, giving us increasing confidence that we are properly exercising each system. There's always more work to do on testing, but it's a substantial improvement.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug causing compiled Quorum programs to load very slowly.")
        ListItem("Input commands now work from the command line, but do not pop-up a window. To make input scalable we have changed the in-IDE behavior as well, now using the standard input box line in NetBeans. This behavior is, we feel, somewhat confusing, but is a tradeoff that fixes a significant bug in Quorum 2.0.")
        ListItem("Added a separate command called input, with no parameters, which allows the user to request input without outputting information first.")
        ListItem("Quorum now requires default values for variables on the inside of actions or in fields. The reason is because Quorum was allowing seemingly rather arbitrary defaults to be selected, which appeared confusing to some users. For example, "):DoubleQuote():Text("boolean a"):DoubleQuote():Text(" could default to either true or false. While we could argue one way or the other, forcing a right-hand-side makes the decision explicit.")
        ListItem("Because of the flexibility of the ALL-STAR algorithm in ANTLR 4, it was relatively easy to fix an issue with negative numbers not correctly parsing under a few (relatively unimportant) circumstances. This was never a major problem, but does make expressions just slightly more flexible and was an annoying bug the team wanted fixed.")
        ListItem("Fixed a number of issues with the way parent actions or fields were called.")
        ListItem("In classes that explicitly declare system actions, the plugin generated is now accessible from inside the plugin architecture. To access it, users can access the variable named plugin_.")
    end

    private action Quorum2_1
        Subsection("Quorum 2.1 December 16th, 2013")
        Card()

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Added a peer review system for Quorum's standard library.")
        ListItem("Added a submission system for the standard library.")
        ListItem("Added a badging system for recognizing users that contribute to Quorum.")
        ListItem("Added an information page on the submission system and process.")
        ListItem("Fixed a broken connection causing the accessibility libraries to not properly show up in the library list.")
        Paragraph("Standard Library and compiler Fixes/Changes")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Fixed a bug causing certain primitive types to not hash correctly.")
        ListItem("Fixed several minor bugs in the standard library.")
        ListItem("Added new data libraries for reading XML files and CSV files.")
        ListItem("Added a number of new additional test cases for various components.")
        ListItem("Fixed a rare verifier error in the compiler.")
        ListItem("Fixed several other small compiler issues.")
    end

    private action Quorum2_0_1
        Subsection("Quorum 2.0.1 August 13th, 2013")
        Card()
        Paragraph("This is a bug fix release for the Quorum 2.0 branch.")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Finished and integrated the Mac OS X version of the accessibility libraries. While the accessibility model on Mac is very different than on PC, the Quorum libraries should work as similarly as we could make them on each platform.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug causing the output buffer to not be cleared correctly on shutdown of a program.")
        ListItem("Fixed a number of bugs in the accessibility libraries.")
        ListItem("This is a Sodbeans release only. We are in the process of fixing one more important bug on the 2.0 branch before we put out a new Quorum installer. As such, those wanting this particular version of Quorum will need to get the updates in Sodbeans.")
    end

    private action Quorum2_0
        Subsection("Quorum 2.0 June 6th, 2013")
        Card()
        Paragraph("Quorum 2.0 includes a host of improvements to the type system, adds the ability to call actions on primitives, includes minor syntactic improvements, and enhances the code completion helper libraries.")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Type System Changes: A number of changes have been made to the type system, finishing off a set of long planned alterations. We hope now that Quorum conforms to the best available empirical evidence. "):Text(" "):Text("A number of changes have been made to the type system, finishing off a set of long planned alterations. We hope now that Quorum conforms to the best available empirical evidence.")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("Actions that return a primitive text value can now return undefined.")
        ListItem("Text primitives can now be assigned as undefined.")
        ListItem("Added the ability to call actions on primitive values. For example, we can now add a colon after an integer and call any action provided by the Object version of the primitive. Generally, this makes it far less necessary to instantiate an object for a primitive type. The solution for this is relatively efficient, as behind the scenes, Quorum calls a static action, with only very slightly more overhead than calling the action on the object.")
        ListItem("Added all of the new type system features into the code completion APIs, meaning that integrated development environments using Quorum, like Sodbeans, should get them for automatically and without alteration.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("Language Additions/Changes:")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("The "):DoubleQuote():Text("print"):DoubleQuote():Text(" keyword has been changed to "):DoubleQuote():Text("output."):DoubleQuote():Text(" This change conforms to data from our surveys with novices, in addition to conforming to common sense. For example, getting input from Quorum required using the word input, but getting output previously required using the word print. This made little sense, as print could have meant printing to a printer, not necessarily printing to a console. This way, input implies input and output implies output, making the language more consistent. All standard library materials, book materials, and curricular materials have been altered for the change.")
        ListItem("Changed the phrase "):DoubleQuote():Text("of type"):DoubleQuote():Text(" in the Error architecture to "):DoubleQuote():Text("is."):DoubleQuote()
        ListItem("Changed the phrase "):DoubleQuote():Text("is a"):DoubleQuote():Text(" in the inheritance system to "):DoubleQuote():Text("is."):DoubleQuote()
        ListItem("Finished a very basic initial version of accessibility APIs for Quorum. This version is largely a proof of concept, but provides some infrastructure calls down to various operating systems and unifies accessibility calls (NSAccessible, IAccessible). This first version is available only for the Windows operating system and only works when using compiled mode. It does not yet function in interpreted mode or on Mac or Linux.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug in the compiler causing extra items to sometimes be wrapped into an output .jar file.")
        ListItem("Added the -server command line flag. This flag turns Quorum into an HTTP server, where code can be sent to it and the output is returned. Additionally, the -server insecure can be called turn off security settings while in this mode. This last mode is not recommended unless the user is running the server locally.")
        ListItem("Added a new flag, -java. This flag allows the user to pass an existing Java jar file to Quorum. When passed, Quorum will automatically wrap any code into the built jar's manifest on compile. This should make it easier for external groups to combine their existing Java code with Quorum projects.")
        ListItem("Finished a significant optimization pass of the compiler. There is always more work that can be done in this area, but a number of the bottlenecks in the Quorum 1.7 branch and earlier have been hammered out.")
        ListItem("Significantly improved the -verify flag, which now gives a much better idea as to which methods have non-compiling, missing, or otherwise broken examples in the documentation.")
        ListItem("Removed the "):DoubleQuote():Text("quote"):DoubleQuote():Text(" token from the language. Now, the text primitive or object can return special character codes by calling actions, including arbitrary unicode values. Helper methods are available for common special characters (e.g., newline, quotes, tabs).")
        ListItem("Lots of bug fixes.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("New Quorum Website"):Text(" "):Text("We have substantially revamped the Quorum website, including adding the ability to run some Quorum programs online and the ability to rate the words/symbols used in the standard library, in an effort to improve them further.")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("The website now has a much improved look and feel.")
        ListItem("The page for finding files in the standard library is now grouped by category, hopefully making it easier to find classes.")
        ListItem("The Quorum website is now easily searchable.")
        ListItem("Users can now login to the website through google or a custom account.")
        ListItem("Pages with documentation generated by the compiler now allow the user to rate various attributes of a class (e.g., the class name, variable names, action names). The user must be logged into to rate.")
        EndNestedList()
    end

    private action Quorum1_7
        Subsection("Quorum 1.7 February 25th, 2013")
        Card()
        Paragraph("Quorum 1.7 adds in a new type inference system, upgrades the internal architecture substantially, and fixes a number of known bugs.")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Quorum now has a type inference system that can be used on the inside of actions (but not in declarations). In effect, this means that users can write phrases like "):DoubleQuote():Text("a = 5"):DoubleQuote():Text(" and the compiler will still statically check, but will allow the type declaration to be excluded under many circumstances. This new system partially completes changes to the Quorum 2.0 type system, which conforms to user studies with humans done by our team and Stefan Hanenberg.")
        ListItem("Substantially altered the static analysis tools internally to Quorum. This greatly increases the quality of the types of tools that can be built on top of the compiler. For example, Sodbeans now has much better code completion support due to this upgrade.")
        ListItem("Added new web libraries for Quorum. This initial version is in beta and will be completed in Quorum 2.0. The current version, located in Libraries.Web supports the HTML 5 specification (or by calling print "):DoubleQuote():Text("my page here"):DoubleQuote():Text("). There are a number of limitations in this first release, but a basic web server can be created by passing the -web tag to the compiler (or in Sodbeans).")
        ListItem("Added a hash table to the standard library under Libraries.Containers.HashTable.")
        ListItem("Added a class for handling bitwise operations to the standard library under Libraries.Compute.BitwiseOperations.")
        ListItem("Made more changes to the compiler errors output by Quorum as part of our continuing mission to make Quorum easier to use.")
        ListItem("Updated and expanded the curriculum and documentation for Quorum.")
        ListItem("Added a way to pass and use command line arguments.")
        ListItem("Fixed a bug with the "):DoubleQuote():Text("me"):DoubleQuote():Text(" keyword.")
        ListItem("Fixed a rare, but critical, bug in the inheritance system.")
        ListItem("Fixed an odd bug in the scoping system.")
        ListItem("Fixed a number of small edge-case bugs.")
    end

    private action Quorum1_6
        Subsection("Quorum 1.6 September 9th, 2012")
        Card()
        Paragraph("Quorum 1.6 contains a number of important bug fixes.")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Fixed a number of bugs with the error system (called exceptions in other languages). These changes include a near rewrite of the bytecode generation algorithms for this system.")
        ListItem("In order to help identify problems in the future, we have added a considerable number of test cases for the errors system. We think these tests offer a much more complete automated suite for this part of the compiler.")
        ListItem("Fixed some bugs in the control flow analysis algorithms. These fixes will not impact the runtime behavior of any Quorum programs, but will make alternative control flow sequences that are illegal or impossible a little bit more obvious.")
        ListItem("Improved the clarity slightly of a few compiler errors. As always, making compiler errors easier to understand is a work in progress.")
        ListItem("Fixed a number of small edge-case bugs.")
    end

    private action Quorum1_5
        Subsection("Quorum 1.5 June 26th, 2012")
        Card()

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Significantly altered the syntax for conditional statements (if). The reason for this change is because we ran an empirical study, which showed evidence that novices using this construct made consistent errors, especially in the use of the token "):DoubleQuote():Text("then"):DoubleQuote():Text(" and "):DoubleQuote():Text("end"):DoubleQuote():Text(" on the inside of else if constructs. There is still one more set of tests we would like to run on this construct, to reveal whether the keywords "):DoubleQuote():Text("else if"):DoubleQuote():Text(" lead to higher accuracy than our current choice, "):DoubleQuote():Text("elseif."):DoubleQuote():Text(" We have not yet discovered clear empirical evidence in the academic literature, so will probably end up running the tests on our own. Below we give a quick example of the change.")
        Paragraph("We previously had the following:")
        CodeExample("if a = b then
end else if c = d then

end else then
end")
        Paragraph("The syntax is now the following:")
        CodeExample("if a = b
elseif c = d

else
end")
        Paragraph("We may change the design of this construct again in the future if we find more, or better, evidence for against any particular design. Users, or other researchers, that have conducted formal empirical studies, with corresponding evidence, that they think might illuminate more decisions here should let us know.")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Made minor changes to check-detect syntax. Like if statements, we removed the inner "):DoubleQuote():Text("end"):DoubleQuote():Text(" statements. We did not run a formal empirical study on this change, but we thought it was a likely conclusion, given the if statement results. Further, this change keeps our language consistent across language constructs.")
        ListItem("We now have a new Quorum Interpreter In internal tests, this includes a speed increase from between 1,100% and 21,000% speed improvement for simple examples. This timing data includes just the speed the interpreter runs, not compilation speed. This interpreter is now used by default if the -interpret flag is used. For example, "):DoubleQuote():Text("quorum -interpret Main.quorum"):DoubleQuote():Text(" would use the new version.")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("In internal tests, this includes a speed increase from between 1,100% and 21,000% speed improvement for simple examples. This timing data includes just the speed the interpreter runs, not compilation speed.")
        ListItem("This interpreter is now used by default if the -interpret flag is used. For example, "):DoubleQuote():Text("quorum -interpret Main.quorum"):DoubleQuote():Text(" would use the new version.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("Added quite a few new compiler tests. These tests have helped us to identify and fix a host of bugs (mostly minor) in the compiler, including a host of edge cases.")
        ListItem("Quorum now has a significantly improved documentation generation system Changed the -document flag so that it now auto-generates HTML5 documentation for Quorum libraries. Added a new flag called -verify, which automatically checks that any "):DoubleQuote():Text("examples"):DoubleQuote():Text(" used in the documentation compile. Updated the online wiki Quorum documentation to the 1.5 syntax. Significantly improved the quality of code examples in Quorum documentation.")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("Changed the -document flag so that it now auto-generates HTML5 documentation for Quorum libraries.")
        ListItem("Added a new flag called -verify, which automatically checks that any "):DoubleQuote():Text("examples"):DoubleQuote():Text(" used in the documentation compile.")
        ListItem("Updated the online wiki Quorum documentation to the 1.5 syntax.")
        ListItem("Significantly improved the quality of code examples in Quorum documentation.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("Fixed a major compiler bug that didn't allow the user to access parent variables.")
        ListItem("Library Changes Completed a total redesign of the File class. We're looking for feedback on this class, but hope that it will be easier to use. Minor bug fixes in the music and sound classes. Fixed a number of bugs in classes like Random and the Containers. Added a new class called Libraries.Sound.Audio, which can playback media files. In this first release, it is designed to make it easy to playback .wav files easily. Future releases will probably expand the functionality further, depending on whether we get any user requests. Added a new set of Robot Control Libraries for interacting with iCreate's CBC robot controller.")
        NestedBulletList()
        ListItem("Completed a total redesign of the File class. We're looking for feedback on this class, but hope that it will be easier to use.")
        ListItem("Minor bug fixes in the music and sound classes.")
        ListItem("Fixed a number of bugs in classes like Random and the Containers.")
        ListItem("Added a new class called Libraries.Sound.Audio, which can playback media files. In this first release, it is designed to make it easy to playback .wav files easily. Future releases will probably expand the functionality further, depending on whether we get any user requests.")
        ListItem("Added a new set of Robot Control Libraries for interacting with iCreate's CBC robot controller.")
        EndNestedList()
        ListItem("Adjusted the design of Compiler error messages. Our changes here are pretty minor, but our goal was to generally make the messages more consistent and obvious to users. users that find error messages that still are not clear should please feel free to file a bug report.")
        ListItem("Lots of bug fixes.")
    end

    private action Quorum1_0
        Subsection("Quorum 1.0 January 30th, 2012")
        Card()
        Paragraph("This is the initial release of the Quorum programming language. Currently, Quorum has the following features:")

        BulletList()
        ListItem("Fully compiled down to Java bytecode")
        ListItem("Static, but flexible, type checking")
        ListItem("Unique control structures, heavily tested to be easy to understand by novices and professionals")
        ListItem("Object-oriented language")
        ListItem("Standard Library (e.g., data structures, music generation, text-to-speech)")
        ListItem("Plugin system for extending Quorum")
        ListItem("Integration with the NetBeans IDE")
        ListItem("Talking Omniscient debugger (The debugger literally talks to you and tells you what is going on).")
    end
end
